Tax Cuts Benefiting Working Americans
=20
=20
=20
=20

Last year, President Donald J. Trump signed into law the Working Families T=
ax Cuts, landmark legislation that ushered in a new era of tax relief and p=
revented the largest tax increase in American history from taking effect. T=
his past filing season over 110 million refunds were issued, and *over 67 m=
illion filers* took advantage of at least one tax break from the Working Fa=
milies Tax Cuts:


  * No tax on tips;=20
  * No tax on overtime;=20
  * No tax on car loan interest (for qualifying vehicles);=20
  * Or an enhanced deduction for America=E2=80=99s seniors.=20

These new provisions enabled working and older Americans to keep more of th=
eir hard-earned money.


  * More than *30 million* workers claimed the *No Tax on Overtime* deducti=
on with an average benefit of *over $3,100*=20
  * More than *38 million* Americans 65 and older claimed the *enhanced sen=
ior deduction* with an average deduction of *over $7,500*=20
  * Nearly *8 million *workers claimed the *No Tax on Tips* deduction with =
an average deduction of *over $7,000*=20
  * *1.5 million* filers claimed the *No Tax on Made-in-America Car Loan In=
terest* with an average benefit of *over $1,800*=20

Americans who claimed these new tax cuts this year received real, meaningfu=
l tax relief. If you did not and may be eligible, here is the good news =E2=
=80=93 the no tax on tips, no tax on overtime, no tax on car loan interest,=
 and the enhanced senior deductions are all in place until at least 2028. F=
or more information about these provisions and eligibility requirements, pl=
ease visit the IRS=E2=80=99s Working Families Tax Cuts website [ https://ww=
w.irs.gov/newsroom/one-big-beautiful-bill-provisions-individuals-and-worker=
s ].

With these new tax cuts in effect, and the dedicated staff at the IRS, we r=
ecently completed the most successful tax filing season in history.


  * The average refund was 11% larger than last year=20
  * 98% of returns were filed electronically=20
  * Over 90% of refunds were issued in less than three weeks=20

Hardworking Americans like you are keeping more of what they earn because o=
f President Trump=E2=80=99s historic tax cuts.

Frank J. Bisignano
Chief Executive Officer
Internal Revenue Service

